*  POKER_driver - drives POKER.SNO, which plays cold-hand five-card poker
*  between two players with nothing wild, and with it the ABCDR, ALPHA, BETA
*  and BET functions the manifest names for this module.  Contract per
*  POKER.sno header.  POKER carries its own END, so a driver can only be the
*  include plus scripted answers on stdin.  See the batch-E FINDING for why
*  no oracle .ref accompanies this driver: POKER needs the four-argument
*  INPUT(.INPUT,5,,'phrases.in') association, which Spitbol refuses with
*  ERROR 116 (and it also includes SQRT.sno, which Spitbol refuses
*  separately with ERROR 248), AND it reaches RANDOM.sno through CARDPAK,
*  which CSNOBOL4 refuses with Error 1, Illegal data type.  Neither
*  sanctioned oracle can run it.
-INCLUDE "POKER.sno"
